n gate of a temple,","it unfolds,","blooms,","and","opens wide,","so that when you come inside,","then,","with enchanted eyes, you may see","yourself,","your own wondrous form!","।2।","Neither does it let go,","nor do I turn off the path and run away;","it builds its nest in the circle of my navel.","The more I think I will understand it,","giving sweat,","giving blood,","entwining life with life,","the more incomprehensible it seems,","patting my back and saying:","my dear!","Poetry is not understood by effort;","it comes to be understood."]],"inline_breaks":[],"hidden_lines":[]}},"end_mark":"leaf","author":"Pravakar Satapathy","route":"poem-22.html","portrait":"assets/writers/41-earth-voice-v3-64.webp","illustration":{"src":"assets/section-art/editorial-desk-poetic-natural.webp","alt":"Blank sheets, pencils and a notebook in soft window light.","width":1536,"height":1024},"availability":""}]}
